WEBVTT

00:00:03.560 --> 00:00:05.270
I'm hungry.

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:07.520
What's for lunch today?

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:21.040
Let's give some romantic advice, shall we?

00:01:51.690 --> 00:01:55.950
This is Fuji Girls' Love Broadcasting Station

00:01:54.300 --> 00:01:56.130
And then, Noriko...

00:01:58.670 --> 00:02:01.300
The student council has a
special broadcast to make today.

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:02.970
Go back to your classrooms.

00:02:03.740 --> 00:02:06.960
But you need prior approval
for special broadcasts...

00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:09.520
We haven't heard anything about this.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:13.790
They might get suspicious,

00:02:14.240 --> 00:02:18.340
but if they do, win them over with that
pleasant attitude you're so proud of.

00:02:18.940 --> 00:02:21.450
I'm sorry. There may have
been a misunderstanding.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:22.950
It's all right, though.

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:25.340
You can trust me.

00:02:25.340 --> 00:02:26.160
Right?

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:28.960
If you say so, President Maki.

00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.640
Hey, wait!

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:32.330
Are you saying you can't trust me?

00:02:32.720 --> 00:02:34.590
Why are you stopping them?

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.720
It's time for the lunchtime broadcast.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:43.480
Today's student council special
broadcast is brought to you by me,

00:02:43.480 --> 00:02:44.510
Maki Natsuo, and...

00:02:44.750 --> 00:02:48.230
Your main DJ, Enomoto Yuiko.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.850
Why are you the main DJ, Enomoto-senpai?

00:02:51.850 --> 00:02:54.670
Because I'm older than you, obviously!

00:02:54.670 --> 00:02:56.640
Yet you're an elementary schooler on the inside...

00:02:56.640 --> 00:02:58.520
What did you say?!

00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:03.360
Excuse us.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.190
Let's try that again.

00:03:05.190 --> 00:03:06.740
The student council has
an announcement to make.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:08.850
What could this be?

00:03:09.200 --> 00:03:10.850
Excuse me.

00:03:10.850 --> 00:03:11.710
What?

00:03:12.260 --> 00:03:15.440
The student council has something
to discuss with the teachers.

00:03:15.760 --> 00:03:16.750
Through Tanahashi-san.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:21.690
Mizushima-senpai, you go to the
faculty office and distract them.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:22.890
However,

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:25.230
Suzu will do the talking.

00:03:27.990 --> 00:03:31.140
What's wrong? Calm down, okay?

00:03:31.460 --> 00:03:32.640
There, there.

00:03:32.640 --> 00:03:34.230
Nothing to be scared of.

00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:36.940
She turned them into
caretakers in an instant.

00:03:37.190 --> 00:03:41.570
I-I can't distract the teachers!

00:03:41.790 --> 00:03:42.850
It's all right.

00:03:42.850 --> 00:03:47.530
What's amazing about you in this plan is
the way you succeed, even when you fail.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.080
I didn't know what she
meant at the time, but...

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.730
I-If you could start by
looking at these documents...

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.100
Hey, wait.

00:04:01.450 --> 00:04:02.290
Tanahashi-san!

00:04:02.290 --> 00:04:03.340
Are you all right?

00:04:05.520 --> 00:04:07.840
My glasses... my glasses...

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:08.810
Calm down.

00:04:08.810 --> 00:04:10.680
Your glasses are on top of your head.

00:04:11.070 --> 00:04:13.660
Oh, I need to pick up my documents.

00:04:13.660 --> 00:04:14.700
It's all right.

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.110
We'll get them.

00:04:16.640 --> 00:04:18.280
I get it now.

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.570
...is what we believe.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:23.150
Next,

00:04:23.820 --> 00:04:25.930
we will answer the question
left in the suggestion box

00:04:25.930 --> 00:04:27.780
on the second floor of the north building.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:28.280
What?

00:04:28.540 --> 00:04:32.200
Natsuo and Yuiko's Heart-Pounding
English Conversation Lesson!

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:36.000
For those of you having trouble
keeping up in your English classes...

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:38.760
The most important thing is to grow
familiar with conversational English,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.330
and to take interest in it.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:44.460
As an example, we'll provide you
with a brief English conversation.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.570
I am Michael, 14 years old.

00:04:46.570 --> 00:04:49.640
There is a girl who is more than
a friend, but not my girlfriend.

00:04:49.860 --> 00:04:51.560
I am John, 15 years old.

00:04:51.560 --> 00:04:52.630
No girlfriend.

00:04:52.630 --> 00:04:54.850
Despite being sort of meek,
I'm popular with girls.

00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.480
What's with that scenario?

00:04:56.480 --> 00:04:58.550
Maki is speaking
in English

00:04:56.690 --> 00:04:58.560
Hey, John. What's up?

00:04:58.580 --> 00:05:03.330
Eno is speaking
in English as well

00:04:58.970 --> 00:05:02.900
Hey, Michael. The present Nancy
gave me yesterday is terrible.

00:05:03.330 --> 00:05:05.970
Oh, what kind of present was it?

00:05:05.970 --> 00:05:09.580
Well, she gave me something
homemade. In this day and age!

00:05:09.580 --> 00:05:11.200
A complete wool outfit, at that.

00:05:11.200 --> 00:05:12.910
What am I, a sheep?

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:17.250
I wore it to sleep, and I
got a rash on my thighs.

00:05:17.570 --> 00:05:19.700
John's a pretty nice guy.

00:05:19.700 --> 00:05:22.910
Yoshida-sensei, you're the broadcasting
club's advisor, aren't you?

00:05:22.910 --> 00:05:24.260
Yes.

00:05:24.420 --> 00:05:27.600
Did you give the student council
permission to make a broadcast today?

00:05:27.820 --> 00:05:29.840
Now that you mention it...

00:05:30.890 --> 00:05:31.970
Sakagami-sensei?

00:05:32.750 --> 00:05:35.720
The present I got from Yuma
was pretty brutal, too.

00:05:35.720 --> 00:05:37.850
It was really expensive.

00:05:37.850 --> 00:05:39.600
Wh-What's wrong with that?

00:05:39.600 --> 00:05:41.940
It means she put that
much love into her gift.

00:05:42.240 --> 00:05:44.610
There's plenty wrong with
it. We're still students.

00:05:45.020 --> 00:05:47.950
I don't like girls who try
to buy you with money.

00:05:48.510 --> 00:05:52.740
She used all her savings to buy me
a giant wood carving of a tsuchinoko.

00:05:52.740 --> 00:05:54.780
What kind of person is Yuma?

00:05:54.780 --> 00:05:56.330
And why a tsuchinoko?

00:05:56.710 --> 00:05:59.260
In short, if you're going to
give someone a present...

00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:02.420
Don't give something
homemade or expensive.

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:05.090
I-Is this...

00:06:05.380 --> 00:06:08.000
Things have finally calmed down.

00:06:08.000 --> 00:06:09.510
I-I'm sorry.

00:06:09.730 --> 00:06:11.850
So, what did you want to discuss?

00:06:12.030 --> 00:06:15.200
What? Oh, um...

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.430
It's written in those documents.

00:06:17.830 --> 00:06:18.520
What?

00:06:18.840 --> 00:06:22.340
Tanahashi-san is a bit reclusive
for a student council member,

00:06:22.340 --> 00:06:25.190
so we wanted to make her
practice talking to people.

00:06:25.810 --> 00:06:28.110
It seems she wasn't ready for it, though.

00:06:28.620 --> 00:06:30.570
Sorry for all the commotion.

00:06:31.040 --> 00:06:32.190
Come on, let's go.

00:06:32.190 --> 00:06:33.040
Huh?

00:06:33.400 --> 00:06:34.470
What?

00:06:37.660 --> 00:06:41.850
Basically, the best thing to
do is ask what we want, right?

00:06:41.850 --> 00:06:43.090
That's right.

00:06:43.760 --> 00:06:45.090
What did you think?

00:06:45.370 --> 00:06:49.120
Doing something takes effort and courage.

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:51.140
But, you can do it.

00:06:51.580 --> 00:06:54.470
The Fuji Girls' student council
supports you with all our hearts!

00:06:56.450 --> 00:06:57.310
Okay!

00:06:57.860 --> 00:06:59.620
What was that?

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:02.020
An English lesson, right?

00:07:03.600 --> 00:07:05.480
Well, I guess that worked out.

00:07:05.480 --> 00:07:08.310
Broadcasting Room

00:07:06.650 --> 00:07:09.990
All that's left is my job.

00:07:10.210 --> 00:07:13.940
We have prepared handouts
summarizing the English conversation.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:17.500
If you'd like one, you can pick one up
from the student council room after school.

00:07:18.040 --> 00:07:21.210
This concludes the student
council special broadcast.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:23.790
Thank you for listening.

00:07:24.220 --> 00:07:26.380
They finished the broadcast
without any trouble.

00:07:26.380 --> 00:07:27.130
Yeah.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.560
I'm sorry about that.

00:07:29.560 --> 00:07:30.840
I didn't do very well.

00:07:30.840 --> 00:07:32.410
No, you were perfect.

00:07:32.410 --> 00:07:34.830
We didn't let anyone leave the faculty office.

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:36.970
But, um...

00:07:37.180 --> 00:07:39.960
Thank you for helping me!

00:07:39.960 --> 00:07:41.600
N-No problem.

00:07:41.600 --> 00:07:43.970
Riko-senpai was right.

00:07:43.970 --> 00:07:47.360
We can always depend on your quick wit!

00:07:53.260 --> 00:07:58.150
Student Guidance Office

00:08:00.080 --> 00:08:01.710
Is something wrong?

00:08:01.710 --> 00:08:03.210
No, nothing.

00:08:03.210 --> 00:08:04.640
Thanks for waiting!

00:08:05.250 --> 00:08:07.880
Did I make it a great success or what?

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:11.230
I could never do something
like that. I'm impressed.

00:08:11.420 --> 00:08:13.730
Huh? Riko's not here.

00:08:13.730 --> 00:08:17.800
She said she'd stand guard outside the
broadcast room, but she wasn't there.

00:08:18.390 --> 00:08:19.930
Where did she go?

00:08:21.140 --> 00:08:23.560
Let's go back to the student council room.

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.280
Riko's taking a long time.

00:08:36.280 --> 00:08:37.870
Sorry, sorry.

00:08:38.190 --> 00:08:40.610
Riko, where have you been?

00:08:40.610 --> 00:08:42.580
I just went to the bathroom.

00:08:42.580 --> 00:08:45.040
I knew it was something like that.

00:08:45.520 --> 00:08:46.710
Sheesh.

00:08:47.140 --> 00:08:49.220
Our romantic advice was a huge success.

00:08:49.450 --> 00:08:50.420
Yeah!

00:08:51.540 --> 00:08:53.050
Oh, no.

00:08:53.050 --> 00:08:55.100
I need to apologize to the
broadcasting club advisor

00:08:55.100 --> 00:08:56.260
for not submitting a request form.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:59.260
I-I already took care of that.

00:08:59.260 --> 00:09:01.810
The advisor's my homeroom
teacher, Yoshida-sensei.

00:09:02.320 --> 00:09:04.290
R-Really?

00:09:04.510 --> 00:09:06.100
Hey, where's your hair tie?

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:09.730
Th-The band snapped.

00:09:10.080 --> 00:09:11.340
I see.

00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:14.070
Riko-senpai, your plan was a huge success.

00:09:14.430 --> 00:09:15.300
Yeah, I guess.

00:09:15.300 --> 00:09:16.910
I was in the right place at the right time.

00:09:17.120 --> 00:09:20.280
Of course, you have my
brilliant performance to thank.

00:09:20.280 --> 00:09:22.740
The student guidance office is the
right place for you, Kurahashi?

00:09:23.670 --> 00:09:25.980
D-Don't say weird stuff like that!

00:09:25.980 --> 00:09:26.880
I didn't.

00:09:26.880 --> 00:09:29.250
I never said you went to the
bathroom in the guidance office.

00:09:29.250 --> 00:09:30.840
Now that's really weird!

00:09:31.310 --> 00:09:32.150
Riko?

00:09:32.150 --> 00:09:36.460
Anyway, your English was
amazing, content aside.

00:09:36.460 --> 00:09:39.140
Do you think you could teach me?

00:09:39.140 --> 00:09:42.060
I'm hoping to score 20 points
higher than I did on the last test.

00:09:42.410 --> 00:09:44.270
Are you going for a perfect score?

00:09:44.270 --> 00:09:46.270
No, lower than that.

00:09:46.580 --> 00:09:47.600
90?

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:48.980
Lower than that.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.260
80?

00:09:50.880 --> 00:09:51.820
Lower.

00:09:52.060 --> 00:09:53.300
70?

00:09:53.620 --> 00:09:54.730
A little lower.

00:09:54.730 --> 00:09:56.280
65?

00:09:56.790 --> 00:09:58.240
K-Keep going...

00:09:58.920 --> 00:10:01.240
I'm surprised you got into
Fuji Girls' with scores like that.

00:10:01.240 --> 00:10:03.660
I studied as hard as I could
for the entrance exams!

00:10:03.660 --> 00:10:05.250
I can do it if I put my mind to it!

00:10:05.790 --> 00:10:07.610
But you can't if you don't, right?

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:09.190
W-K!

00:10:09.190 --> 00:10:10.200
Riko!

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:14.580
The Next Day

00:10:19.170 --> 00:10:20.600
This looks good.

00:10:20.600 --> 00:10:22.000
Are you looking for study materials?

00:10:22.650 --> 00:10:23.760
Sakagami-sensei.

00:10:24.040 --> 00:10:25.460
I'm impressed.

00:10:25.460 --> 00:10:27.760
I hope Kurahashi-san
learns something from you.

00:10:27.760 --> 00:10:30.470
I heard she was bothering
you again yesterday.

00:10:30.470 --> 00:10:32.190
I don't know what to do with her.

00:10:32.460 --> 00:10:33.330
What?

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:35.580
What are you talking about?

00:10:37.390 --> 00:10:38.900
Studying, huh?

00:10:39.460 --> 00:10:40.820
How depressing.

00:10:41.350 --> 00:10:42.400
Hey.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:49.410
Wh-What's going on?

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:51.750
Riko.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.210
What really happened yesterday?

00:10:55.520 --> 00:10:57.170
N-Nothing.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:10:58.930
Don't play dumb!

00:10:58.930 --> 00:11:02.660
Someone saw you get dragged into
the student guidance office!

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:04.290
That was you!

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:06.960
Riko, this conversation isn't over.

00:11:06.960 --> 00:11:08.850
But she...

00:11:09.150 --> 00:11:09.940
Riko.

00:11:11.610 --> 00:11:12.560
Okay.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:16.920
What are you doing?

00:11:16.920 --> 00:11:19.890
And to broadcast such vulgar content!

00:11:19.890 --> 00:11:21.860
It's to improve my English.

00:11:21.860 --> 00:11:24.990
Normal content is so boring,
I never remember it.

00:11:25.320 --> 00:11:27.740
You didn't get permission
to use the broadcast room.

00:11:28.150 --> 00:11:29.880
Oh, whoops!

00:11:29.880 --> 00:11:32.140
Maki asked me to do it, but I forgot.

00:11:32.140 --> 00:11:33.460
Sorry.

00:11:34.950 --> 00:11:36.580
In any case, we should stop this at once!

00:11:36.580 --> 00:11:37.610
Don't!

00:11:37.970 --> 00:11:40.720
If you suddenly stop the broadcast,
people will think it's weird.

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:42.690
You'll ruin Maki's image.

00:11:42.690 --> 00:11:44.280
This is your fault!

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.530
Come with me.

00:11:45.530 --> 00:11:47.840
You're wearing a garish hair tie again too, I see.

00:11:47.960 --> 00:11:49.060
Yoshida-sensei!

00:11:49.340 --> 00:11:50.980
Don't stop the broadcast!

00:11:51.190 --> 00:11:55.840
It's to, um, improve everyone's English!

00:11:56.180 --> 00:11:57.520
Really? Okay, then.

00:11:58.980 --> 00:12:01.410
I look forward to your next English test.

00:12:01.630 --> 00:12:03.280
I hope you'll raise your score by 20 points.

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:04.250
What?!

00:12:04.250 --> 00:12:05.750
Come on, let's go.

00:12:08.120 --> 00:12:09.560
And so...

00:12:09.730 --> 00:12:11.460
Well, you got me!

00:12:11.820 --> 00:12:14.170
Did you plan that from the start?

00:12:14.940 --> 00:12:16.790
You know how I am.

00:12:16.790 --> 00:12:19.580
It wouldn't have been as
convincing coming from you.

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:22.120
I really was the right person for the job.

00:12:23.680 --> 00:12:24.580
Suzu.

00:12:24.580 --> 00:12:25.550
Yes.

00:12:26.470 --> 00:12:27.870
Ow!

00:12:28.110 --> 00:12:30.210
But it worked, right?!

00:12:30.210 --> 00:12:31.980
And I'm used to having teachers yell at me!

00:12:32.220 --> 00:12:34.040
That's not the problem!

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:35.980
I can't forgive you for sacrificing yourself!

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.920
Why not?

00:12:37.920 --> 00:12:39.700
You used to do everything yourself—

00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:40.650
That's why!

00:12:41.210 --> 00:12:45.130
You were the one who told
me to rely on others.

00:12:45.380 --> 00:12:49.010
But you... you...

00:12:51.820 --> 00:12:53.240
I'm sorry.

00:12:54.090 --> 00:12:56.010
You won't do it again, right?

00:12:56.010 --> 00:12:57.000
Yeah, yeah.

00:12:57.000 --> 00:12:58.500
Answer only once!

00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:00.210
Yes.

00:13:05.880 --> 00:13:06.850
I'm sorry.

00:13:06.850 --> 00:13:08.800
I forgot to submit a request.

00:13:08.800 --> 00:13:09.680
What?

00:13:09.680 --> 00:13:11.930
You made that simple mistake?

00:13:12.260 --> 00:13:13.530
Despite how I seem,

00:13:13.530 --> 00:13:15.520
I actually make a lot of mistakes.

00:13:15.670 --> 00:13:20.320
But when Kurahashi-san saw me
make a truly embarrassing blunder,

00:13:20.740 --> 00:13:23.820
she cheered me up, saying she had
made the same mistake before.

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:29.450
In that regard, I hope I can
learn to be more like her.

00:13:31.380 --> 00:13:34.430
I need to apologize to Kurahashi-san.

00:13:36.210 --> 00:13:38.550
I'm going to tutor you toward
getting a perfect score.

00:13:38.550 --> 00:13:40.420
Why are you raising the bar?

00:13:40.700 --> 00:13:42.460
You can do it if you put
your mind to it, right?

00:13:42.670 --> 00:13:44.340
You can do it if you put
your mind to it, right?

00:13:44.580 --> 00:13:47.150
You can do it if you put your
mind to it, Riko-senpai!

00:13:47.150 --> 00:13:48.300
I'm sorry!

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:51.050
I was lying!

00:13:52.050 --> 00:13:53.660
The motto of Fuji Girls' is

00:13:53.660 --> 00:13:57.640
"Teach at the student's own pace
and respect her individuality," right?

00:13:58.000 --> 00:13:59.760
Yes, it is.

00:14:02.810 --> 00:14:05.220
Given your individually poor English ability,

00:14:05.220 --> 00:14:07.250
I'll beat it into you at your own pace.

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:10.120
What an open-ended teaching philosophy.

00:14:10.120 --> 00:14:12.820
Your grades are poor,
right? It can't be helped.

00:14:12.820 --> 00:14:14.650
You're a member of the student council.

00:14:14.650 --> 00:14:16.710
That doesn't matter.

00:14:17.080 --> 00:14:18.660
Yes, it does.

00:14:18.660 --> 00:14:21.000
Maki and Suzu are at the
top of their classes.

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.130
Oh, my.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:25.220
The weather's nice today.

00:14:25.220 --> 00:14:28.090
Don't change the subject
without mentioning me!

00:14:28.090 --> 00:14:30.480
I've maintained my high class ranking!

00:14:30.480 --> 00:14:31.760
So have I.

00:14:33.220 --> 00:14:35.470
English is your worst subject, right?

00:14:39.490 --> 00:14:41.580
The weather is very nice today.

00:14:41.580 --> 00:14:43.610
Stop! Your kindness hurts!

00:14:43.820 --> 00:14:47.040
There's been a change in my idiot ranking.

00:14:45.190 --> 00:14:48.140
Idiot Ranking
Student Council
Treasurer's Findings
1. Riko
2. Maki
3. Eno

00:14:47.040 --> 00:14:48.070
What?

00:14:49.490 --> 00:14:51.420
I'm not in it!

00:14:51.590 --> 00:14:53.450
You should be happy about that.

00:14:53.970 --> 00:14:57.130
I know I'm an idiot.

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.390
You can do it if you put your mind to it.

00:15:00.060 --> 00:15:02.670
Let's work hard together, my sweetie.

00:15:07.420 --> 00:15:09.260
Don't die, Huggy!

00:15:09.490 --> 00:15:11.010
What do you think you're doing?

00:15:11.330 --> 00:15:13.820
I thought you'd feel like hitting the books

00:15:13.820 --> 00:15:15.450
if we pretended he was teaching you.

00:15:15.450 --> 00:15:17.680
I did feel like hitting <i>him.</i>

00:15:16.240 --> 00:15:17.680
"Hit" the Books

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:19.820
I still love you, even if you're violent!

00:15:19.820 --> 00:15:22.080
His characterization isn't the issue.

00:15:22.080 --> 00:15:24.770
I think he's gross because he's a hug pillow.

00:15:25.680 --> 00:15:27.230
In that case, I have just the thing.

00:15:30.040 --> 00:15:31.960
He doesn't look like a pillow now.

00:15:31.960 --> 00:15:33.820
You made him even worse!

00:15:34.060 --> 00:15:35.990
Why do you have that uniform, anyway?

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.280
We had some funds leftover...

00:15:38.450 --> 00:15:40.990
But it felt too real, so I got embarrassed

00:15:40.990 --> 00:15:42.040
and put it in storage.

00:15:44.400 --> 00:15:45.660
I know it's a little late,

00:15:45.660 --> 00:15:48.170
but I can't believe I let this girl
become the council president.

00:15:48.250 --> 00:15:52.210
Idiot Ranking
Student Council
Treasurer's Findings
1. Maki
2. Riko
3. Eno

00:15:48.450 --> 00:15:51.100
I'm happy to announce Maki
has taken first place.

00:15:51.100 --> 00:15:52.500
All right!

00:15:53.560 --> 00:15:56.030
But to think that's how you've
been spending our funds...

00:15:56.450 --> 00:15:57.930
Shall we step outside?

00:15:57.930 --> 00:16:00.060
No!

00:16:00.280 --> 00:16:02.770
It'll be good for you to be scolded for once.

00:16:04.180 --> 00:16:06.140
Would you like some tea?

00:16:06.140 --> 00:16:06.980
Sure.

00:16:11.760 --> 00:16:14.150
I don't care much for Huggy,

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:17.730
but I guess I can work hard if a
pretty boy's willing to teach me.

00:16:17.730 --> 00:16:19.370
There you go again.

00:16:20.080 --> 00:16:23.420
Let's study, Kurahashi-san.

00:16:24.950 --> 00:16:25.960
Wh-What?

00:16:26.250 --> 00:16:28.090
I am Maki Makio.

00:16:28.380 --> 00:16:29.470
Nice to meet you.

00:16:30.840 --> 00:16:32.610
It was going to waste,
so I put it to use.

00:16:32.610 --> 00:16:33.980
Don't do that!

00:16:33.980 --> 00:16:35.680
A-Are you stupid?

00:16:37.850 --> 00:16:40.870
Your hair is just like cotton candy.

00:16:41.940 --> 00:16:43.920
I've always thought of you
like a younger sister,

00:16:43.920 --> 00:16:45.970
but you're a lady now, huh?

00:16:46.380 --> 00:16:49.500
She's had no shortage of fantasies
about her ideal boyfriend,

00:16:49.500 --> 00:16:51.610
and she's damn good at reenacting them...

00:16:51.980 --> 00:16:55.140
Well, it's time for our lesson, Riko.

00:16:55.320 --> 00:16:56.210
Stay away!

00:16:56.210 --> 00:16:57.700
Lay off the crossdressing and I'll study!

00:16:58.050 --> 00:17:00.240
Sh-She's offering to help. Why not?

00:17:00.460 --> 00:17:01.220
What?

00:17:01.220 --> 00:17:03.350
I-I'll help you.

00:17:03.350 --> 00:17:04.040
What?!

00:17:04.510 --> 00:17:06.670
I'll help you every day until your test.

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:12.540
Someone help me!

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.040
After the Test

00:17:14.340 --> 00:17:16.050
My test came back!

00:17:16.240 --> 00:17:19.220
I've never scored so high
on an English test before.

00:17:19.510 --> 00:17:20.500
Look!

00:17:21.430 --> 00:17:23.770
That's amazing.

00:17:21.450 --> 00:17:23.760
Scores Are Always 90~100

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:25.340
Always in the 80s

00:17:24.170 --> 00:17:25.350
Way to go.

00:17:26.620 --> 00:17:28.060
Riko!

00:17:30.080 --> 00:17:32.540
Now that our romantic
advice and test are over,

00:17:32.540 --> 00:17:33.990
things are finally calming down.

00:17:33.990 --> 00:17:37.530
I hope things went well for
the girl who asked our advice.

00:17:37.640 --> 00:17:38.410
Yeah.

00:17:38.510 --> 00:17:40.410
Present

00:17:40.410 --> 00:17:41.850
Date

00:17:41.850 --> 00:17:43.270
Abduction

00:17:43.270 --> 00:17:44.770
Chase

00:17:44.770 --> 00:17:46.220
Final Battle

00:17:46.230 --> 00:17:47.770
Showdown

00:17:47.770 --> 00:17:52.330
Grand Finale

00:17:48.420 --> 00:17:49.920
How wonderful.

00:17:49.920 --> 00:17:52.340
Your fantasies have evolved, haven't they?

00:17:52.340 --> 00:17:55.300
I want to fall in love so badly,
I think I'm going crazy!

00:17:55.530 --> 00:17:59.030
Riko, how do you fall
in love with someone?

00:17:59.240 --> 00:18:01.510
What? W-Well...

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.890
Ask someone who has a boyfriend!

00:18:04.630 --> 00:18:06.550
Huh? Boyfriend?

00:18:06.550 --> 00:18:07.890
Don't forget about him.

00:18:07.890 --> 00:18:09.020
Poor guy.

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.450
Yeah, but he was the
one who approached me.

00:18:12.450 --> 00:18:13.980
I just gave in to his advances.

00:18:13.980 --> 00:18:19.440
14 Years of Rejection

00:18:15.770 --> 00:18:17.030
Is something wrong?

00:18:17.030 --> 00:18:19.450
I thought you had lots of people
approaching you, Kurahashi-san.

00:18:19.930 --> 00:18:22.790
How did you meet him
while attending Fuji Girls'?

00:18:22.790 --> 00:18:25.800
Our school is girls-only from
preschool to high school.

00:18:25.800 --> 00:18:28.930
Sayo went to a public school for a while.

00:18:28.930 --> 00:18:29.750
Really?

00:18:30.110 --> 00:18:32.250
So, why did he first approach you?

00:18:33.470 --> 00:18:35.380
Well, if I have to name a reason...

00:18:37.920 --> 00:18:38.950
Because he saw my underwear?

00:18:38.950 --> 00:18:41.930
I was an idiot for
expecting a normal answer.

00:18:42.140 --> 00:18:43.610
Wh-What kind of underwear?!

00:18:43.610 --> 00:18:44.560
Don't ask her that!

00:18:44.560 --> 00:18:46.810
I-I think I could handle leggings...

00:18:47.000 --> 00:18:52.360
My brother said, "It's utterly disappointing to
see a girl who's so oblivious as to wear leggings!"

00:18:52.360 --> 00:18:52.910
What?

00:18:52.910 --> 00:18:54.390
You've got a lot to learn.

00:18:54.390 --> 00:18:57.280
I'm utterly disappointed in your brother.

00:18:57.280 --> 00:19:00.660
I could wear panties over leggings!

00:19:00.660 --> 00:19:02.120
Why would you do that?

00:19:02.120 --> 00:19:03.410
Do you get that from your father?

00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:05.080
My father has nothing to do with this!

00:19:05.370 --> 00:19:07.450
Please don't fight!

00:19:07.960 --> 00:19:11.230
My brother said he likes leggings.

00:19:11.230 --> 00:19:13.170
I'm sick of your brothers.

00:19:13.560 --> 00:19:15.920
Wasn't there a more normal reason?

00:19:15.920 --> 00:19:17.940
You sat next to each other,

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:19.460
or you were in the same club,

00:19:19.460 --> 00:19:21.260
or you had mutual friends...

00:19:24.160 --> 00:19:27.520
Master Riko, you know a
lot of boys, don't you?

00:19:27.950 --> 00:19:29.480
Y-Yeah.

00:19:29.480 --> 00:19:31.060
Well, um...

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:33.720
Do you know anyone like Huggy?

00:19:33.720 --> 00:19:34.770
If I did, I'd beat him up.

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:37.340
D-Do you know anyone like Makio?

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:38.680
You're an angel!

00:19:37.340 --> 00:19:38.690
If I did, I'd run away!

00:19:38.690 --> 00:19:41.600
Wild Kid Makio Wakio

00:19:38.930 --> 00:19:40.960
Do you know anyone like Wakio-senpai?

00:19:40.960 --> 00:19:41.610
Who?

00:19:41.610 --> 00:19:43.410
Do you know anyone rich?

00:19:43.410 --> 00:19:45.530
Don't you feel bad for your boyfriend?

00:19:46.470 --> 00:19:51.370
The boys I know are all in love with me.

00:19:51.370 --> 00:19:53.750
You'd only get hurt!

00:19:53.980 --> 00:19:56.070
Hurting the
most right now.

00:19:56.110 --> 00:19:57.950
The Next Day

00:19:59.030 --> 00:19:59.880
It's an emergency!

00:20:00.690 --> 00:20:01.970
What's wrong, Suzu?

00:20:02.210 --> 00:20:05.600
W-We got a response in the suggestion box.

00:20:05.800 --> 00:20:06.380
What?

00:20:06.380 --> 00:20:07.760
Seriously?

00:20:09.940 --> 00:20:13.520
"Dear student council members,
thank you very much.

00:20:13.820 --> 00:20:16.190
Regarding the matter I asked you about,

00:20:16.470 --> 00:20:18.310
the result was...

00:20:20.740 --> 00:20:22.320
Defeat.

00:20:24.640 --> 00:20:27.120
H-He and I..."

00:20:27.560 --> 00:20:29.410
I'll read it.

00:20:30.520 --> 00:20:32.650
"He and I attended the
same elementary school,

00:20:32.650 --> 00:20:34.330
and we don't get to
see each other often.

00:20:34.560 --> 00:20:36.560
While choosing a gift
for him at the store,

00:20:36.560 --> 00:20:37.820
I ran into him.

00:20:37.820 --> 00:20:41.320
Remembering your advice
to ask him what he likes,

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.800
I gathered up my courage
and spoke to him.

00:20:44.100 --> 00:20:47.970
It had been a while since we had talked
so much on the way home together.

00:20:47.970 --> 00:20:49.570
It made me happy.

00:20:49.860 --> 00:20:52.860
However, he seems to have a girl he likes.

00:20:53.020 --> 00:20:56.100
I was sad at first, but I
felt better after crying."

00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.300
I was naïve.

00:20:59.460 --> 00:21:02.150
Not everything will go well.

00:21:02.570 --> 00:21:04.530
Our advice was useless.

00:21:05.100 --> 00:21:06.920
There's another page.

00:21:08.190 --> 00:21:11.810
"Now that I can think about it calmly,
he doesn't have a girlfriend yet.

00:21:11.810 --> 00:21:13.910
I shouldn't give up yet."

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:14.750
What?

00:21:15.900 --> 00:21:18.440
"I understand him better now,

00:21:18.440 --> 00:21:20.550
and can use that knowledge
in my next strategy."

00:21:20.840 --> 00:21:21.920
Resilient girl.

00:21:22.310 --> 00:21:25.090
"I am able to think this
way because of you.

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:26.920
Thank you again!"

00:21:27.060 --> 00:21:28.430
That's that!

00:21:30.860 --> 00:21:32.470
All right!

00:21:32.470 --> 00:21:34.380
You can do it!

00:21:35.740 --> 00:21:37.850
I want to fall in love!

00:21:39.190 --> 00:21:41.400
Sure, but be careful.

00:21:41.400 --> 00:21:43.660
If someone finds out a
student council member

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:45.660
is breaking Fuji Girls' ban
on romantic relationships,

00:21:45.660 --> 00:21:47.780
it won't end well.

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:49.910
You're one to talk.

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:52.290
What should we do if she
asks us for more advice?

00:21:52.290 --> 00:21:54.950
We can't use a broadcast again.

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:57.830
No one's that weird.

00:21:57.850 --> 00:22:00.570
These handouts summarize the English lesson
from the lunchtime broadcast! Please take one.
Student Council President
Maki Natsuo

00:21:58.140 --> 00:21:59.730
There they are.

00:21:59.730 --> 00:22:02.960
Aren't these the handouts
from today's broadcast?

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:10.300
Hey, didn't you think that
broadcast was kind of strange?

00:22:10.300 --> 00:22:11.880
Yeah, I did.

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:14.790
And at the last student meeting...

00:22:17.030 --> 00:22:20.150
I think things are about to
get interesting, Nana-chan.

00:22:20.150 --> 00:22:21.090
Yes.

00:22:21.090 --> 00:22:24.070
It smells like something's
cooking, Momo-senpai.

00:23:57.810 --> 00:24:03.610
Preview

00:23:58.590 --> 00:24:01.450
The student council special broadcast: overtime!

00:24:01.450 --> 00:24:03.150
We have less than 30 seconds, though.

00:24:03.150 --> 00:24:05.500
It's like when you announce there's more to come,

00:24:05.500 --> 00:24:07.350
but it comes back from commercials
and immediately ends.

00:24:07.350 --> 00:24:10.720
Our first request song is
"Both Sleeping and Awake, Lingerie!"

00:24:11.050 --> 00:24:13.280
How long are you going to keep that joke going?

00:24:13.280 --> 00:24:15.090
Okay, Maki's dad, take it away.

00:24:14.860 --> 00:24:18.300
Both sleeping and awake, lingerie.

00:24:15.090 --> 00:24:16.060
Is that actually him?

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:20.160
Hearing someone who usually acts
stupid coming up with retorts is great.

00:24:18.300 --> 00:24:22.000
My brain is shaped like a bra.

00:24:20.160 --> 00:24:24.130
I've never seen Riko-senpai
look so happy before.

00:24:22.000 --> 00:24:27.150
My heart is a G-string.

00:24:23.500 --> 00:24:27.140
The Terrible Legend of Riko

00:24:27.150 --> 00:24:30.140
Don't miss the next episode!
